// The provider interfaces of UI Automation the Windows backend implements, for the MicroCom
// generator (src/tools/MicroCom.CodeGenerator).
//
// The reference has no interface definition file for them: it declares each interface in C#
// (`Interop/I*.cs` of its automation project) for the COM source generator of its runtime. This
// file is written from those declarations: every interface with its identifier and its methods
// in the order of the declaration, which is the order of the virtual function table, under the
// names of the reference (`GetProviderOptions` where the header of the system has the property
// `ProviderOptions`). The enumerations and the identifiers of properties, patterns, events and
// control types are the ones the reference declares beside the interfaces.
//
// Compared with `UIAutomationCore.idl` of the Windows SDK (through the declarations of the
// `windows` crate, which are generated from the metadata of the SDK: the identifier and the
// names of the slots of all 25 interfaces, by a script): the identifiers and the order of the
// methods are the ones of the system for every interface here. Two declarations of the reference
// differ from the header, and this file follows the header for the first:
//   - `ITextProvider::RangeFromPoint` takes a `UiaPoint` by value in the header and two doubles
//     in the reference. The two are the same call on 32-bit x86 and on ARM64, and are not on
//     x86-64, where a structure of sixteen bytes is passed by reference. No class of the
//     reference implements the interface, so nothing there is called through it.
//   - the member `Rotatation` of the property identifiers is `UIA_RotationPropertyId` (30166):
//     the value is the one of the system, the name is the one of the reference.
// The reference also leaves out what the header added after it was written (the provider
// options above `UseComThreading`, the events after `Changes`): nothing here uses them.
//
// The lines below name the Rust type of every type name the file does not declare.
@rust-types-from super
@rust-map BOOL i32
@rust-map HWND isize
@rust-map LPCWSTR *const u16
@rust-map BSTR *mut u16
@rust-map VARIANT crate::automation::marshalling::ComVariant
@rust-map SAFEARRAY_PTR crate::automation::marshalling::SafeArrayRef

[flags]
enum ProviderOptions
{
    ClientSideProvider = 0x0001,
    ServerSideProvider = 0x0002,
    NonClientAreaProvider = 0x0004,
    OverrideProvider = 0x0008,
    ProviderOwnsSetFocus = 0x0010,
    UseComThreading = 0x0020
}

